look (1) the rdetail line gives tomato_sauce's inputs; if they are not 2 tomatoes the pot never starts: BATCH-FAULT, rerun with those inputs. (2) first pot be line (unlit, 200 ticks): CookTime 0. (3) after BurnTime 400 the oven reads lit=true; 240 ticks later the pot's CookTime > 0 or the sauce is in slot 6/8. (4) after the burn ran out (481 ticks after the merge) lit=false and the two last pot be lines 80 ticks apart show the same CookTime (no progress). (5) last oven inv still holds slot 0 potato x3 (checked). data get line: note the fuel slot index (ItemHandler) for the CQ / a rerun with real fuel

## SQ-CMP-11 | A full corpse turns skeleton 7 days after death, caught up on load
@group A
@commands Shortened `[corpses] skeletonTime = 200` and a restart (stands in for 7 days); `forceload add 0 0`; advance the clock 300 ticks; `summon corpse:corpse 2 -60 2 {Tags:["c11a"],Death:{PlayerName:"Test",MainInventory:[{Slot:0b,id:"minecraft:stone",Count:1b}]},"creativecompat:corpse":{DeathTime:1L}}` and a second with `Tags:["c11b"]` and no `creativecompat:corpse`; wait 3 s; read each `Stage`
@pass c11a: `Stage: 1b` (skeleton; its death was more than skeletonTime ticks of game time ago); c11b: `Stage: 0b` with a `DeathTime` near the current game time
@fails c11a stays 0: the decay check does not run (tick redirect or config gate); c11b turns skeleton at once: DeathTime defaulted to 0
@jars creativecompat
@sources feature_writeup/plan_corpses.md
@tier T2
@reviewed 2026-11-20
@absent creativecompat:corpse (an NBT compound key on the corpse entity, not a registry id)
# r1120fix (2026-11-20): a negative DeathTime is the mixin's "unset" sentinel (CorpseDecayMixin: deathTime < 0 -> now - age),
# so the r1120nv fixture read as just died. Now: skeletonTime 200 ticks (restart), the clock moved past 300 ticks, and a
# positive DeathTime 1 (game tick 1); the default is put back at the end of the row
edit python3 "$INST/tools/scratch_query/qrun.py" toml config/creativecompat-common.toml corpses skeletonTime 200
restart
> forceload add 0 0
sleep 3
> cdevtest tickwarp 300
waitlog verb=tickwarp end=done ticks=300 120
> time query gametime
capture GT The time is (\d+)
> summon corpse:corpse 2 -60 2 {Tags:["c11a"],Death:{PlayerName:"Test",MainInventory:[{Slot:0b,id:"minecraft:stone",Count:1b}]},"creativecompat:corpse":{DeathTime:1L}}
> summon corpse:corpse 4 -60 2 {Tags:["c11b"],Death:{PlayerName:"Test",MainInventory:[{Slot:0b,id:"minecraft:stone",Count:1b}]}}
sleep 3
> data get entity @e[tag=c11a,limit=1] "creativecompat:corpse".Stage
expect has the following entity data: 1b
> data get entity @e[tag=c11b,limit=1] "creativecompat:corpse".Stage
expect has the following entity data: 0b
> data get entity @e[tag=c11b,limit=1] "creativecompat:corpse".DeathTime
look c11b DeathTime is near the game time {GT} (within a few hundred ticks), not 0
> kill @e[tag=c11a]
> kill @e[tag=c11b]
shell python3 "$INST/tools/scratch_query/qrun.py" toml config/creativecompat-common.toml corpses skeletonTime 168000
reject (Unknown or incomplete command|Incorrect argument for command|No entity was found|\[cdevtest\] verb=tickwarp .*done=0)

## SQ-CMP-13 | Nether: skeleton after 1 day, wither skeleton after 2; End: never
@group A
@commands Shortened Nether times (`netherSkeletonTime = 200`, `netherWitherTime = 200`: wither 200 ticks after the skeleton) and a restart; advance the clock 600 ticks; in the Nether a corpse holding stone (`c13a`) with `DeathTime` 300 ticks ago, a second (`c13b`) with `DeathTime:1L`; in the End a third (`c13c`) with `DeathTime:1L`; forceload each spot; wait 3 s; read each `Stage`
@pass c13a 1b, c13b 2b, c13c 0b
@fails c13b 1b: the Nether list does not match the dimension id; c13c 1b: the End is not in `noDecayDimensions`
@jars creativecompat
@sources feature_writeup/plan_corpses.md
@tier T2
@reviewed 2026-11-20
@absent creativecompat:corpse (an NBT compound key on the corpse entity, not a registry id)
# r1120fix (2026-11-20): a negative DeathTime is the mixin's "unset" sentinel (CorpseDecayMixin: deathTime < 0 -> now - age),
# so the r1120nv fixture read as just died. Now: Nether skeleton at 200 ticks, wither 200 ticks later (stand in for 1 + 1 days;
# restart), the clock moved 600 ticks, positive DeathTimes; the defaults (24000 / 24000) are put back at the end of the row
edit python3 "$INST/tools/scratch_query/qrun.py" toml config/creativecompat-common.toml corpses netherSkeletonTime 200 && python3 "$INST/tools/scratch_query/qrun.py" toml config/creativecompat-common.toml corpses netherWitherTime 200
restart
> execute in minecraft:the_nether run forceload add 0 0
> execute in minecraft:the_end run forceload add 100 0
sleep 5
> cdevtest tickwarp 600
waitlog verb=tickwarp end=done ticks=600 120
> time query gametime
capture GT The time is (\d+)
> execute in minecraft:the_nether run summon corpse:corpse 0 64 0 {Tags:["c13a"],NoGravity:1b,Death:{PlayerName:"Test",MainInventory:[{Slot:0b,id:"minecraft:stone",Count:1b}]},"creativecompat:corpse":{DeathTime:{GT-300}L}}
> execute in minecraft:the_nether run summon corpse:corpse 2 64 0 {Tags:["c13b"],NoGravity:1b,Death:{PlayerName:"Test",MainInventory:[{Slot:0b,id:"minecraft:stone",Count:1b}]},"creativecompat:corpse":{DeathTime:1L}}
> execute in minecraft:the_end run summon corpse:corpse 100 64 0 {Tags:["c13c"],NoGravity:1b,Death:{PlayerName:"Test",MainInventory:[{Slot:0b,id:"minecraft:stone",Count:1b}]},"creativecompat:corpse":{DeathTime:1L}}
sleep 3
> execute in minecraft:the_nether run data get entity @e[tag=c13a,limit=1] "creativecompat:corpse".Stage
expect has the following entity data: 1b
> execute in minecraft:the_nether run data get entity @e[tag=c13b,limit=1] "creativecompat:corpse".Stage
expect has the following entity data: 2b
> execute in minecraft:the_end run data get entity @e[tag=c13c,limit=1] "creativecompat:corpse".Stage
expect has the following entity data: 0b
> execute in minecraft:the_nether run kill @e[tag=c13a]
> execute in minecraft:the_nether run kill @e[tag=c13b]
> execute in minecraft:the_end run kill @e[tag=c13c]
shell python3 "$INST/tools/scratch_query/qrun.py" toml config/creativecompat-common.toml corpses netherSkeletonTime 24000 && python3 "$INST/tools/scratch_query/qrun.py" toml config/creativecompat-common.toml corpses netherWitherTime 24000
look c13a must read 1b (its death {GT}-300 lies between the skeleton at 200 and the wither at 400 ticks); the three Stage lines in order a, b, c
reject (Unknown or incomplete command|Incorrect argument for command|No entity was found|\[cdevtest\] verb=tickwarp .*done=0)
